(4777154, 685679, 60862, '<td valign="top">In response to your thread asking for comments, I would''ve scored this a 6 or 7, which is a good score from me.  I like the yellow color, the skyline, and the pure silhouette.  The skyline''s seems a little soft, so try F/8 or F/11 next time.  Also, and this just my preference, I like photos where the subject''s either dead center or well away from it.  Here, the composition feels like there''s too much on one side or the other.</td>', 'In response to your thread asking for comments, I would''ve scored this a 6 or 7, which is a good score from me.  I like the yellow color, the skyline, and the pure silhouette.  The skyline''s seems a little soft, so try F/8 or F/11 next time.  Also, and this just my preference, I like photos where the subject''s either dead center or well away from it.  Here, the composition feels like there''s too much on one side or the other.', '2008-06-20 02:09:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(4777157, 685679, 93883, '<td valign="top">I really like this idea, and the picture you took is really cool.  It is a little busy though, I wonder if you could play with the perspective a little.  If you could get the fountain to appear larger and maybe limit the background to just the skyscrapers, possibly by shooting from a lower angle, that might give the picture some more focus.  Don''t know if you could get such a shot from that location, but it might be worth a try.  Congratualtions on a new PB!</td>', 'I really like this idea, and the picture you took is really cool.  It is a little busy though, I wonder if you could play with the perspective a little.  If you could get the fountain to appear larger and maybe limit the background to just the skyscrapers, possibly by shooting from a lower angle, that might give the picture some more focus.  Don''t know if you could get such a shot from that location, but it might be worth a try.  Congratualtions on a new PB!', '2008-06-20 02:11:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(4777319, 687192, 22180, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by MaryO:</b></div><hr/><i> Looks like an interesting place to explore. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Central Anatolia: Graves carved into the rocks (B.C. 1200 - 800)</td>', 'Originally posted by MaryO: Looks like an interesting place to explore.  Central Anatolia: Graves carved into the rocks (B.C. 1200 - 800)', '2008-06-20 06:42:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(4777459, 685679, 36006, '<td valign="top">The idea was fantastic, but the left and right of your crop was distracting and cumbersome for me.<br/> <br/>If there was a way to just see the city scape, even up to the Disney Auditorium, and cropped away the buildings that didn''t do anything for the image, and kept the same idea going, I think your image would of done better.</td>', 'The idea was fantastic, but the left and right of your crop was distracting and cumbersome for me. If there was a way to just see the city scape, even up to the Disney Auditorium, and cropped away the buildings that didn''t do anything for the image, and kept the same idea going, I think your image would of done better.', '2008-06-20 10:20:22.000000', NULL, 0),
